                            <p class="text-gray-700 font-semibold">Understanding the Workflow:</p>

                            <div class="bg-blue-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-400">
                                <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm"><strong>Task: generate_data</strong> - Creates dummy FASTQ files locally. Uses Python container. Takes num_samples and output_dir as inputs and outputs an array of FASTQ files using glob pattern.</p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="bg-blue-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-400">
                                <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm"><strong>Task: quality_assessment</strong> - Runs inside a Python Docker container. Filters sequences based on quality scores. The <code class="bg-gray-200 px-1 rounded">String output_filename</code> line dynamically creates output names based on input filename.</p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="bg-blue-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-400">
                                <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm"><strong>Task: alignment</strong> - Also containerized. Takes an array of filtered FASTQ files and produces one alignment results file. Uses <code class="bg-gray-200 px-1 rounded">${sep=' ' filtered_fastqs}</code> to join multiple files with spaces.</p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="bg-blue-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-400">
                                <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm"><strong>Workflow: bioinformatics_pipeline</strong> - Orchestrates the pipeline:
                                <ul class="list-disc ml-4 mt-2">
                                    <li><code class="bg-gray-200 px-1 rounded">scatter (fastq in generate_data.fastq_files)</code> - Parallelizes quality assessment: creates one quality_assessment task for each FASTQ file</li>
                                    <li><code class="bg-gray-200 px-1 rounded">quality_assessment.filtered_fastq</code> - In scatter context, this becomes an array of filtered files</li>
                                    <li><code class="bg-gray-200 px-1 rounded">call alignment { input: filtered_fastqs = quality_assessment.filtered_fastq }</code> - Waits for all scatter jobs to complete, then passes all results to alignment</li>
                                    <li><code class="bg-gray-200 px-1 rounded">output { ... }</code> - Declares workflow outputs that users can reference</li>
                                </ul>
                                </p>
